WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.748 --> 00:00:07.527
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> OK Team B. You have one minute to ask Team A questions.

2
00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:12.153
<v><b>George:</b></v> Mmm let’s start with Nadine. Mike’s your hairdresser, right?

3
00:00:12.382 --> 00:00:15.740
<v><b>Nadine:</b></v> Yes, we’re very good friends.

4
00:00:16.351 --> 00:00:18.366
<v><b>George:</b></v> What’s the name of his salon?

5
00:00:18.504 --> 00:00:24.076
<v><b>Nadine:</b></v> Er, it’s called er… Good Hair Day.

6
00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:28.412
<v><b>Charlie:</b></v> Is Mike married?

7
00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:31.130
<v><b>Nadine:</b></v> Er, yes he is.

8
00:00:32.107 --> 00:00:34.046
<v><b>Alice:</b></v> Does he have children?

9
00:00:34.183 --> 00:00:41.298
<v><b>Nadine:</b></v> Er, yes, er, no, he doesn’t. I don’t think he has children.

10
00:00:41.344 --> 00:00:47.664
<v><b>Alice:</b></v> OK, so now Tyler. You say Mike’s your dentist. Where is his clinic?

11
00:00:47.832 --> 00:00:51.603
<v><b>Tyler:</b></v> It’s er in central London, in Piccadilly.

12
00:00:52.046 --> 00:00:54.107
<v><b>Charlie:</b></v> Are you and Mike friends?

13
00:00:54.229 --> 00:01:02.076
<v><b>Tyler:</b></v> Well no, not really friends. It’s difficult to be friends with your dentist – it’s impossible to have a conversation!

14
00:01:04.183 --> 00:01:06.229
<v><b>George:</b></v> Is he expensive?

15
00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:08.977
<v><b>Tyler:</b></v> What do you think? He’s a dentist!

16
00:01:10.275 --> 00:01:16.626
<v><b>George:</b></v> OK, James now. You say Mike’s a chef in a pub. What’s the name of the pub?

17
00:01:16.718 --> 00:01:18.962
<v><b>James:</b></v> The Red Lion. It’s a great pub.

18
00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.832
<v><b>Charlie:</b></v> What food does Mike cook?

19
00:01:21.893 --> 00:01:27.206
<v><b>James:</b></v> Er, Great British food! Fish and chips, roast beef, things like that.

20
00:01:27.496 --> 00:01:29.954
And he makes good sandwiches.

21
00:01:30.015 --> 00:01:32.306
<v><b>Alice:</b></v> What’s his speciality?

22
00:01:32.328 --> 00:01:34.191
<v><b>James:</b></v> Er, spaghetti carbonara.

23
00:01:36.481 --> 00:01:39.351
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> OK, team. Your time’s up.